\f0\fs24 \cf0 # README ------------------------------------------------------------------------\
# Generated on: 2025-12-08\
\
# GENERAL INFORMATION -----------------------------------------------------------\
# Title of Analysis: Monte Carlo Simulation of Spatial Dependence and Standard Errors\
# Institution: Anonymous\
# Date of data generation: 2025-12-08\
\
# SHARING / ACCESS INFORMATION --------------------------------------------------\
# Data source: Synthetic spatial panel data generated entirely within the script.\
# County boundaries come from the R maps package and the county list from\
# data/CountyDistrictList.csv. No other external or proprietary datasets are used.\
\
# DATA & FILE OVERVIEW ----------------------------------------------------------\
# Project folder: Spatial-Dependence-Monte-Carlo\
#\
# script_files/\
#   - spatial_se_sim.R : full simulation workflow including data construction,\
#     spatial weighting, Monte Carlo loop, estimation (OLS, Conley, SEM), and plotting.\
#   - functions.R : helper functions (mrnorm for correlated normal draws, conley for\
#     Conley standard errors), sourced by spatial_se_sim.R.\
#   - out.RDS : saved simulation results; loaded instead of rerunning the simulations if present.\
#\
# data/\
#   - CountyDistrictList.csv : list matching each county to its agricultural statistics district.\
#\
# output_figure/\
#   - OLS_verses_SEM_Spatial_Dependence.png : density comparisons for OLS vs. SEM\
#     coefficients and standard errors under spatial dependence.\
#\
# Relationship: The script constructs spatially dependent panel data, runs repeated\
# simulations, computes multiple forms of standard errors, and visualizes sampling\
# distributions.\
\
# METHODOLOGICAL INFORMATION ----------------------------------------------------\
# Simulation settings:\
#   - Number of counties: n = 958\
#   - Time periods: 2005\'962009 (T = 5)\
#   - Replications: nsims = 750\
#   - Spatial autocorrelation parameter: rho = 0.95\
#   - Error variance: sig2.u = 25\
#   - True parameters: beta = (1, 1)\
#\
# Data generating process:\
#   - Spatial weights: k-nearest neighbors (k=10), inverse-distance weights.\
#   - x2: spatially dependent regressor (multivariate normal with Sigma).\
#   - x1: independent normal noise scaled to match sd(x2).\
#   - alpha: individual fixed effects drawn from N(50, 30).\
#   - Errors: spatially dependent disturbances generated using mrnorm().\
#   - Outcome: y = X*beta + alpha + e.\
#\
# Estimation:\
#   - OLS (within estimator), Conley (distance-based) SEs, and SEM (spatial error model).\
#   - Conley kernels: cutoffs = 0\'96500 miles in increments of 100.\
#   - Outputs: coefficients and SEs across all replications.\
#\
# Software Requirements:\
#   - R >= 4.x\
#   - Packages: spdep, plm, splm, RColorBrewer, maps, maptools, raster,\
#               data.table, geosphere, foreign, reshape, parallel, lfe,\
#               plyr, sf (all installed automatically if missing).\
#\
# Reproducibility: Random seeds are set using set.seed() throughout.\
\
# DATA-SPECIFIC INFORMATION -----------------------------------------------------\
# OLS_verses_SEM_Spatial_Dependence.png:\
#   - Density plots for sampling distributions of OLS vs. SEM coefficients.\
#   - Middle row: SEM standard errors vs. true SD of sampling distribution.\
#   - Bottom row: Conley SEs across distance cutoffs for both regressors.\
#\
# Notes:\
#   - All data are synthetic.\
#   - No missing values.\
#   - Output is saved automatically as out.RDS for reuse.\
#\
# END OF README ----------------------------------------------------------------\
}